<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dream Pool Essays</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1088</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Dream Torrent Essays, Meng Xi Bi Tan, Brush Talks from a Dream Brook, Brush Talks from Dream Brook</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dream Pool Essays (Meng Xi Bi Tan, in full Brush Talks from a Dream Brook) is an encyclopedic book by the Chinese polymath and statesman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shen-kuo">Shen Kuo</a>, published in 1088 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a>. Shen compiled it in forced retirement on his estate near modern Zhenjiang and named it after the estate. Its observations range over medicine, mathematics, astronomy, optics, engineering, metallurgy, early archaeology and fossils, from which Shen reasoned that climates had changed. It holds the first record of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnetic-compass">compass</a> used for navigation and the first description of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bi-sheng">Bi Sheng</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">movable type</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a>. Originally 30 chapters, it was reorganised into 26 in an edition of 1166.</p></div>
